{
  "comment": [
    "Shared composer contract for task B4-3 slice S1. One file, three consumers:",
    "`flutter_app/test/live_source_composer_test.dart`, `Tests/live-foundation/main.swift` and",
    "`Tests/webos/live_source_composer.test.js`. Each reads these bytes and asserts the same outcomes, so a",
    "value pinned on one port is pinned on all three.",
    "",
    "This directory is deliberately new instead of `tests/fixtures/live_catalog/`: only `Tests/` is tracked in",
    "git (`git ls-files` shows no lowercase `tests/` path), and the owner's APFS volume and the macOS runners",
    "are case-insensitive, so creating `tests/` next to `Tests/` would name one directory twice. It is also not",
    "inside `Tests/fixtures/multi-source/`, whose README freezes that group as the five-file M3U parse contract",
    "that three suites read as one set.",
    "",
    "Placeholder hosts only (`cdn.example`, `stream.example`, `img.example`). No real stream address,",
    "credential, or authorized-source list belongs here. The one token-bearing address is a synthetic refusal",
    "probe: `SECRETVALUE` is not a secret and must never reach a composed row."
  ],

  "builtInPlaylistId": "builtin:live",
  "builtInProviderNamespace": "famelack",

  "rows": {
    "comment": [
      "Built-in rows use the flat runtime row shape (`nanoid`, `name`, `streams`, `languages`, `country`,",
      "`isGeoBlocked`), which is what each port's host type holds: Swift wraps `streams` in `LiveTVStreams`,",
      "Dart passes it to `LiveTvChannel`, and on webOS these are already `normChannel` outputs.",
      "",
      "Names are ASCII on purpose. The three ports sort with three different host comparators (I3: Swift",
      "`localizedCaseInsensitiveCompare`, Dart `toLowerCase().compareTo`, webOS lowercased `<`) and the brief",
      "forbids unifying collation, so an order-sensitive fixture with Persian names would pin one port's",
      "collation rather than the composer. The `languages` and `label` fields still carry non-ASCII text."
    ],
    "builtIn": [
      {
        "nanoid": "irib1",
        "name": "IRIB 1",
        "streams": ["https://cdn.example/irib1.m3u8"],
        "languages": ["fas"],
        "country": "IR",
        "isGeoBlocked": false
      },
      {
        "nanoid": "jamtv",
        "name": "Jam TV",
        "streams": ["https://cdn.example/jamtv.m3u8", "https://cdn.example/jamtv.mp4"],
        "languages": ["fas"],
        "country": "IR",
        "isGeoBlocked": false
      },
      {
        "nanoid": "manoto",
        "name": "Manoto",
        "streams": ["https://cdn.example/manoto.m3u8"],
        "languages": ["fas"],
        "country": "IR",
        "isGeoBlocked": true
      }
    ],
    "foldGap": [
      {
        "nanoid": "presstv",
        "name": "Press TV (720p)",
        "streams": ["https://cdn.example/presstv.m3u8"],
        "languages": ["fas", "eng"],
        "country": "IR",
        "isGeoBlocked": false
      }
    ]
  },

  "expectationKeys": {
    "rowCount": "how many rows the composer returns",
    "names": "the returned rows' `name` values, in returned order",
    "rowStreams": "per row name, the exact stream list the composer must return for that row",
    "rowCountry": "per row name, the `country` the returned row must carry",
    "rowLanguages": "per row name, the `languages` the returned row must carry",
    "rowGeoBlocked": "per row name, the `isGeoBlocked` the returned row must carry",
    "mintedNanoid": "per row name, the exact `nanoid` a composer-minted row must carry",
    "issueCounts": "per issue code, how many issues carry it; an absent code means zero",
    "neutral": "true when the composed rows must be element-for-element the input rows, not merely equivalent; a case without this key asserts the opposite, that its rows must differ from its input, so a document that silently stopped meaning anything fails its own suite instead of passing it"
  },

  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "absent-document",
      "comment": [
        "No stored catalog at all: the state argument is null. The output must be the input rows, same order,",
        "same names, same stream lists, no issues. This is the whole behaviour-neutrality claim for a device",
        "that has never written a catalog."
      ],
      "rows": ["builtIn"],
      "document": null,
      "expect": {
        "rowCount": 3,
        "names": ["IRIB 1", "Jam TV", "Manoto"],
        "rowStreams": {
          "IRIB 1": ["https://cdn.example/irib1.m3u8"],
          "Jam TV": ["https://cdn.example/jamtv.m3u8", "https://cdn.example/jamtv.mp4"],
          "Manoto": ["https://cdn.example/manoto.m3u8"]
        },
        "rowCountry": { "IRIB 1": "IR", "Jam TV": "IR", "Manoto": "IR" },
        "rowLanguages": { "IRIB 1": ["fas"], "Jam TV": ["fas"], "Manoto": ["fas"] },
        "rowGeoBlocked": { "IRIB 1": false, "Jam TV": false, "Manoto": true },
        "issueCounts": {},
