      "id": "corrupt-document",
      "comment": [
        "Storage holds bytes this build cannot decode. The persistence seam reports `corrupt` and hands back no",
        "state, so the caller composes with null and the list is exactly today's. The seam-level half of this",
        "case (the stored text survives untouched and nothing is written) is asserted through each port's real",
        "store, because that is where the refusal happens; `rawDocument` is stored verbatim and never parsed."
      ],
      "rows": ["builtIn"],
      "rawDocument": "{oops",
      "expect": {
