    {
      "id": "duplicate-name-merged",
      "comment": [
        "The user's own playlist re-lists IRIB 1 under a different provider id. Similarity alone never merges",
        "— that is the identity module's load-bearing rule — so the document carries what the user actually",
        "wrote: `associateChannels` records the pair in `logicalIdByMemberId` (the authoritative mapping the",
        "view follows) and an `associations` row that states the member order inside the merged channel.",
        "",
        "Both the built-in half and the mapping are written out literally rather than as a placeholder for a",
        "hash, because the composer anchors a row to its built-in member by provider identity",
        "(`playlistId` + `providerNamespace` + `providerChannelId`) and dedups the members it registers the same",
        "way. So a document that already states the built-in member keeps its own id untouched, and no port has",
        "to duplicate `stableKeyHash` output inside this file.",
        "",
        "Expected outcome: still three rows, not four, and the IRIB 1 row carries both addresses, built-in first",
        "because that is the order the association records. `unifiedMemberCount` states what the unified layer",
        "holds for that channel — assertable on the document by itself here, because both members and the",
        "mapping are already in it."
      ],
