      "id": "user-only-row",
      "comment": [
        "A member the user added that belongs to no built-in row and to no association. It contributes a new",
        "row, and the row must sort where the host comparator puts it — first, here — rather than being",
        "appended, which is what makes the result agree with a list the user would recognize.",
        "",
        "A minted row has no host-side evidence to inherit, so it takes exactly what the catalog states:",
        "`displayName`, `countryCode`, `languages`, the logical channel id as its row identity (never empty, so",
        "`stringId` keeps working), and `isGeoBlocked` false, because nothing here has proven a geo-block.",
        "Nothing invents a logo or a capability.",
        "",
        "`mintedNanoid` pins that identity to `member:user-bbc`: `logicalIdOf` gives an unassociated member its",
        "own id, and the document states the mapping literally, so the expectation is a key this file already",
        "carries rather than a hash a port would have to reproduce."
      ],
