    {
      "id": "user-only-row-mid-list",
      "comment": [
        "`user-only-row`, except the minted row's name sorts between two built-in names instead of before all",
        "of them. The pair matters together: a composer that prepends minted rows passes the first and fails",
        "this one, and a composer that appends them is the other way round. Only placing the row where the host",
        "comparator puts it satisfies both.",
        "",
        "The built-in rows keep their own input order, because the composer inserts rather than re-sorting: an",
        "unstable host sort applied to two same-named rows could swap their stream lists between refreshes, and",
        "that would be a behaviour change S1 is not allowed to introduce."
      ],
